WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.038
Step ten breaks it on purpose.

2
00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:05.855
Append a word to the drift
summary inside day two's package,

3
00:00:05.855 --> 00:00:09.275
and verify it: the file doesn't
match its hash, an error.

4
00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:12.122
Compare the days the
wrong way round: refused,

5
00:00:12.122 --> 00:00:15.738
because the current run isn't
later than the previous one.

6
00:00:15.738 --> 00:00:17.800
Each refusal exits with one.

7
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.800
And the sample workflow that would run
all this on a schedule lints clean.

8
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.588
Step eleven runs the tests in both shells.

9
00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:27.992
In PowerShell, the evidence
tests, thirty-two pass,

10
00:00:27.992 --> 00:00:30.899
then the whole suite,
three hundred thirty.

11
00:00:30.899 --> 00:00:35.875
In the POSIX shell, pytest in the drift
pipeline: a hundred forty-two pass.

12
00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:40.400
The path's verification log notes that
this suite needs the whole repository,

13
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.450
not just the drift pipeline folder.

14
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.000
Then delete the output
folder in both places,

15
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.020
because they hold the
fixture's privileged holders.
